{
  "dom_id": "step-q330651",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\u03a6(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ compute $P(Z<1.94).$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-2.0\\,$ | $\\,0.0224\\,$ | $\\,0.0217\\,$ | $\\,0.0212\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.9\\,$ | $\\,0.0274\\,$ | $\\,0.0268\\,$ | $\\,0.0262\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.8\\,$ | $\\,0.0344\\,$ | $\\,0.0336\\,$ | $\\,0.0329\\,$ |\n\n$P(Z<1.94)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/0316b85ed769fd2688538ed2c9a47236db0890bf52bf7fcbad021f7d509373b4.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z\u223cN(0,1)$ we have the following symmetry property for $a>0:$\n\n$$\nP(Z>-a)=P(Z<a)=\u03a6(a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z<1.94).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/e708b9dc6927a17f193c216f1b14b1b9ef98e6d9d26a998790112863661ca5d0.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z>-1.94).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/43f1e2eb5354cbdcd5ff359985048fa2d6411167ad5f50fe45c730642e184b61.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z<1.94) & =P(Z>-1.94) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<-1.94) \\\\  & =1-\u03a6(-1.94) \\\\  & =1-0.0262 \\\\  & =0.9738.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
